WHAT TO LOOK FOR (RIPS):
- Verbatim copying (exact same words) without attribution
- Nearly verbatim (only 1-3 word changes) without attribution
- Same sentence structure + same key phrases + only minor word changes without attribution
- Minor rearrangements that keep most of the same words (e.g., "In response, in April" → "In April")
- Removing/adding small words while keeping same structure (e.g., "he had first raised" → "he first raised")
- Minor word substitutions in phrases (e.g., "in just one" → "during one") when rest is nearly identical
- Significant portions (5+ consecutive words) matching verbatim or with only 1-2 word changes

WHAT NOT TO FLAG (NOT RIPS):
- Sentences with attribution (quotation marks, "according to", source mention)
- Legitimate paraphrasing (different wording/phrasing, even if structure is similar)
- Same facts presented with different structure and different words
- Sentences that only share common words or factual information

